# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# Previously this file pinned only `*.py`. Everything else -- the workflows,
# the Dockerfiles, the compose file, the JSON goldens and fixtures, uv.lock,
# the shell and PowerShell scripts under scripts/ -- was left to whatever each
# contributor's `core.autocrlf` happened to be (Git for Windows defaults that
# to `true`, which checks out CRLF and commits CRLF back). Pinning the Python
# sources and nothing else protects the sources and leaves every other file
# free to flip.
#
# The failure mode is not hypothetical and not limited to source files. A tool
# that regenerates a file wholesale -- a lockfile updater, a schema dumper,
# anything writing through a Windows text-mode file handle -- rewrites every
# line ending in the file. The result is a whole-file diff for a few changed
# values, which buries the real change, destroys `git blame`, and can leave the
# file's byte length unchanged so that a size check does not notice.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the index and checks out LF in the working
# tree on every platform, regardless of local configuration, so that class of
# churn becomes unrepresentable.
#
# LF specifically, for every extension including the PowerShell under scripts/:
# the test and publish workflows run on Linux runners and the service is built
# and run in a Linux container, where a stray CR breaks a shebang or a heredoc.
# `scripts/test-in-docker.ps1` is already LF and PowerShell reads LF fine on
# both Windows and Linux, so it is pinned to what it already is rather than
# churned to CRLF. The whole index is already LF, so this renormalises nothing.
#
# Binary files are detected by `text=auto` and copied byte-for-byte. No binary
# file is tracked here today (`git ls-files --eol` reports no `-text` blob);
# the Swiss ephemeris data files are fetched at CI time into the ignored
# `data/ephe/`, never committed. Declare `binary` explicitly alongside any
# binary asset a future change does track, rather than relying on the
# first-8000-bytes NUL heuristic.
#
# tests/test_line_endings.py is the guard: it fails if any tracked path stops
# being covered by this rule, or if any blob is ever stored CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
